@* alignItemWithTrigger, with the switch shadcn puts beside it. On — the default — the list opens
   with the chosen row sitting over the trigger, so the value you already have does not move under
   the pointer. Off, the list hangs below the control like a menu.

   The switch writes the attribute the select reads, so the state lives in the DOM rather than in
   a variable: with scripting off the page still shows whichever state the server rendered. *@
<div class="flex w-full max-w-64 flex-col gap-4">
    <Field Orientation="horizontal" Class="w-fit">
        <Switch id="sa-toggle" checked data-toggles="sa-size"
                data-toggles-attribute="data-align-item-with-trigger"
                data-toggles-on="true" data-toggles-off="false" />
        <FieldLabel For="sa-toggle">Align Item</FieldLabel>
    </Field>

    <Select id="sa-size" name="fruit" aria-label="Fruit">
        <SelectItem Value="apple">Apple</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="banana" Selected>Banana</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="blueberry">Blueberry</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="grapes">Grapes</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="pineapple">Pineapple</SelectItem>
    </Select>
</div>
